{
  "fixture_name": "swift-swiftui-mini",
  "language": "swift",
  "description": "SwiftUI + Combine app: a Package.swift executable target, a Codable model, two Views, an ObservableObject view-model, and a URLSession/Combine service. Exercises struct/class member extraction, property wrappers (@StateObject, @State, @Published, @Environment), intra-file and cross-file CALLS, and per-file IMPORTS. Expectations written for #6273 — this directory carried src/ and no expected.json since it was added, so it produced no report and was graded by nothing.",
  "selection_rule": "Every member DECLARED in the source is gated must_exist, at the kind and name the rest of this corpus already uses: a type is SCOPE.Component (a View is SCOPE.UIComponent), its properties are SCOPE.Schema named <Owner>.<property>, its methods and initializers are SCOPE.Operation named bare. PROPERTIES, not 'stored properties' — an earlier draft said stored, which gated the computed `usersPublisher` while omitting the computed `body` on both Views and the `init` on the view-model, all four of which are equally declared and equally un-emitted. Declared-ness is the line, not storage; a rule that turns on storage would have to un-gate usersPublisher, which is the weaker choice. Nothing here is nice_to_have.",
  "known_wrong_edges_not_expressible": "`fetchAll CALLS decode` is emitted today and is wrong: the `.decode(type:decoder:)` in fetchAll is Combine's publisher operator, and it binds to User.decode only because that is the sole `decode` declared in this tree. must_exist would lock the mis-binding in; nice_to_have would award it credit for being wrong; forbidden_relationships is the right shape but is scored as always-fatal (internal/quality/diff.go counts any match as a ForbiddenHit and scripts/quality/ratchet.py fails on forbidden_hits > 0), so a currently-emitted wrong edge cannot be recorded there without turning the gate red. Recorded here only, in prose the harness ignores. Same for the `http:POST:/` endpoint whose path should be /users — that one IS gated below, as a miss on the correct name, because the correct spelling is derivable from the source rather than invented.",
  "expected_entities": [
    { "name": "App", "kind": "SCOPE.Component", "source_file": "Package.swift", "must_exist": true, "note": ".executableTarget(name: \"App\", path: \"Sources/App\")" },

